Cell["\<\
The two 1-arrays come first, shorter dimensions before longer. The three \
2-arrays follow, all of dimensions 2\[Times]2, separated by symmetry. The \
3-array comes last.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"41ec0a79-e13a-864c-9d0c-5fbbd244cef3"],

Cell["\<\
Because the order is canonical, the same arrays given differently produce the \
identical expression:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0917fbd5-be23-bc47-a9c9-7e245b633dc3"],

Cell["\<\
Hypermatrix[{ArrayObject[{1, 2}], ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}]}] ===
 Hypermatrix[{ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}], ArrayObject[{1, 2}]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a4b703a7-5687-1741-9b1e-b298fe5e9da7"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"37fd0c03-ab18-1749-9ad7-b8e11f3c2e2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Two arrays alike in order, dimensions and symmetry are put in the Wolfram \
Language's own canonical order, so that a hypermatrix is a function of the \
set of arrays it was given and of nothing else. Without that last tiebreak \
the three 2\[Times]2 arrays above could come out in either of two orders \
depending on how they were typed."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"04d08daf-4cc4-6e43-aac2-6b79baf424c9"],

Cell["What goes in", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7701fc73-3de4-6549-b846-550fd715f5b7"],

Cell["\<\
Raw entries are promoted to array objects, and arrays of any kind of entry \
sit together:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"34f50ca4-c945-6146-98b9-0b03f07757dd"],

Cell["\<\
Hypermatrix[{{1, 2}, {1.5, 2.5}, GenerateSymbolicArray[a, {2, 2}]}][\"Domains\
\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f5f12725-2ff7-f342-bf0e-7cd24228cdfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Expression\"\>"}],
   "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"cfb0dc88-bbab-c74f-bafe-33b463c67269"],

Cell["\<\
Length gives the number of arrays, HypermatrixArrays gives them, and Normal \
gives their entries in the same order:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"03a2cf49-b2e1-5548-a85d-ddc298269886"],

Cell["\<\
hm2 = Hypermatrix[{{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}, {1, 2}}];
{Length[hm2], Normal[hm2]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"50d53419-587c-f54a-b990-0a36adabebd7"],

