Cell["5. Drawing arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"294f5ace-ce83-2d43-9abb-c29d8aa32968"],

Cell["\<\
There are two families of pictures, and an array of any order may be drawn in \
either. The flat family gives plane graphics throughout; the spatial family \
gives cubes arranged in space. Which to use is a matter of what you want to \
see, not of what the array is.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d3ece7a-4466-c148-8902-e4622c33155d"],

Cell["The flat family: ArrayGraphics", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fcf9b015-2b9c-dd4a-8685-1315e38ad460"],

Cell["At order one a row of cells, at order two a grid:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e0870ea1-5533-9f4a-ab1d-24b29410749d"],

Cell["\<\
{ArrayGraphics[{1, 2, 3, 4}], ArrayGraphics[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fc61bbf9-efbf-8743-85e5-d526fb6c96a1"],

